MILESTONES = [
 (1826, "Nicéphore Niépce makes the oldest surviving photograph from his window in France. The exposure takes hours."),
 (1839, "Louis Daguerre announces the daguerreotype. The word “photography” is coined the same year."),
 (1839, "Robert Cornelius takes what's often called the first photographic selfie, in Philadelphia."),
 (1841, "William Henry Fox Talbot patents the calotype: a paper negative you can print again and again."),
 (1843, "Anna Atkins publishes the first book illustrated with photographs, using the cyanotype (blue) process."),
 (1851, "Frederick Scott Archer's wet collodion process makes sharp glass negatives that can be copied."),
 (1855, "Roger Fenton photographs the Crimean War, one of the first wars to be photographed."),
 (1861, "The American Civil War begins; Mathew Brady's team and Alexander Gardner photograph it for the nation."),
 (1872, "Eadweard Muybridge starts photographing galloping horses to settle a famous bet."),
 (1878, "Muybridge's Horse in Motion shows that a galloping horse really does have all four hooves off the ground."),
 (1880, "The first photograph is printed in a newspaper using the halftone process."),
 (1888, "George Eastman launches the Kodak camera: “You press the button, we do the rest.”"),
 (1890, "Jacob Riis publishes How the Other Half Lives, using flash photographs of New York's poorest streets."),
 (1900, "The $1 Brownie camera puts photography into children's hands."),
 (1907, "The Lumière brothers sell Autochrome plates: the first practical color photographs."),
 (1914, "Oskar Barnack builds the first Leica prototype, the model for small 35mm cameras."),
 (1935, "Kodak introduces Kodachrome, a color film with rich, lasting colors."),
 (1935, "The US government's Farm Security Administration begins photographing the Great Depression."),
 (1936, "Life magazine launches and puts photographs at the center of the news."),
 (1947, "Photographers including Robert Capa and Henri Cartier-Bresson found the Magnum agency."),
 (1948, "Edwin Land's Polaroid camera produces a finished photograph in about a minute."),
 (1968, "Apollo 8 astronauts photograph Earthrise over the Moon."),
 (1969, "Apollo 11 astronauts take pictures of each other on the Moon."),
 (1975, "Kodak engineer Steven Sasson builds the first digital camera. It weighs eight pounds and records black-and-white pictures to a cassette tape."),
 (1990, "Adobe Photoshop is released, and the Hubble Space Telescope is launched."),
 (2000, "The first camera phones go on sale in Japan."),
 (2007, "The iPhone arrives, and soon a good camera fits in every pocket."),
 (2022, "The James Webb Space Telescope releases its first images of faraway galaxies."),
]
